# Lullabeast container environment (deploy/.env).
#
#   cp .env.example .env    then paste your key on the OPENROUTER_API_KEY line,
#   and uncomment/fill any of the optional settings below that you need.
#
# .env is read by docker compose (env_file) and passed into the container.
# It is gitignored; never commit it.

# ── Provider API key (OPTIONAL at boot: set it, or enter it in the dashboard) ──
# You do not have to set a key here. Leave it blank and the container boots into
# setup mode and the dashboard collects the key (see deploy/README.md, "First
# boot without a key"). Setting it here skips setup mode and takes precedence.
# The shipped model defaults are OpenRouter models, so OPENROUTER_API_KEY is
# the golden path: paste your key after the "=" below. (No cloud key at all is
# needed if you run a local model server; see LOCAL_MODEL_URL below.)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── Local models on the host (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# A local model server replaces the cloud-key requirement at boot: set this and
# you do not need a cloud key. Point it at a model server running on the docker
# host (Ollama, llama.cpp, LM Studio) via the host.docker.internal bridge.
# The server must listen on 0.0.0.0, not 127.0.0.1: a loopback-bound server is
# invisible to containers. Firewall it from everything else.
# Then assign roles with the *_MODEL variables below using local/<model-id>
# values (see the commented example there); see deploy/README.md, "Local models
# on the host".
#LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# The boot probes the server for each model's context window, reasoning, and
# vision support and writes a complete openclaw.json entry. What the server
# cannot report, these set explicitly (they win over probed values and any
# hand-edit, and apply to the *_MODEL-assigned local models). Set REASONING=1
# for a reasoning model the probe could not detect (llama.cpp, LM Studio), or
# 0 to pin it off. VISION declares image input (the executor, reviewer, and
# prd-creator need a multimodal model). CONTEXT_WINDOW also re-derives the
# output budget when MAX_TOKENS is not set. Leave any of them unset to trust
# the probe.
#LOCAL_MODEL_MAX_TOKENS=16384
#LOCAL_MODEL_REASONING=1
#LOCAL_MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
#LOCAL_MODEL_VISION=1

# ── Per-agent model overrides (optional; defaults shown) ────────────────────
# One knob per agent role, also editable post-setup from the dashboard's
# Settings screen (values set here are pinned and win over dashboard edits).
# The executor, reviewer, and prd-creator models must accept image input
# (screenshot-based visual review on UI/INT phases; Ideas chat attachments);
# the boot doctor fails a text-only reviewer or prd-creator before any run
# can spend on it. Defaults are the audited picks from deploy/CONFIG-AUDIT.md.
#PLANNER_MODEL=openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.2
#EXECUTOR_MODEL=openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code
#REVIEWER_MODEL=openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code
#PRD_MODEL=openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code
#ROADMAP_MODEL=openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.2
#ESCALATION_MODEL=openrouter/qwen/qwen3.6-27b
# With LOCAL_MODEL_URL set above, point a role at a local model with a
# local/<model-id> value, e.g.:
#ESCALATION_MODEL=local/qwen3.5-27b

# ── Dashboard port (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Published to the host's loopback only (127.0.0.1:<UI_PORT>).
#UI_PORT=18790

# ── Git identity for pipeline commits (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# The pipeline commits inside your project repos. Defaults: "Lullabeast"
# <lullabeast@container.invalid>.
#GIT_USER_NAME=
#GIT_USER_EMAIL=
